{"ts":"2026-08-20T12:29:22.877Z","type":"quest-declared","sealed":{"doneWhen":{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"operation-ledger-self-move-waiter-fairness-v3","consecutive":3,"metric":"priority"}},"frontierMetrics":[{"probe":"scenario-harness","args":{"scenario":"operation-ledger-self-move-waiter-fairness-v3","metric":"priority"}}],"authoringContractVersion":1,"statement":"A disruptive operation-ledger self-move that observes incumbents publishes one durable PENDING intent before waiting, preventing later dependent admissions from overtaking it; physical dispatch remains parked until typed authoritative owner visibility proves the ledger idle, and unreadable visibility canonically retries. Existing operation-owner recovery, run-20 exclusivity, run-22 quorum spread, emergency ADD, remove safety, topology fences, numeric budgets, and the 60-second five-node bar remain unchanged. Red-on-revert explicitly observes the legacy refusal, admits later newcomers while the writer is unregistered, and fails the named no-overtake assertion; fixed bytes pass that proof and the fairness model.","title":null,"class":"product","constraints":[{"id":"source-change-subagent-verification","statement":"If this Quest changes source code, spawn a subagent verifier before audit and git handoff, then record a Solver finding with evidence subagent:<id>."},{"id":"durable-owner-visible-intent","statement":"The waiting turn remains the existing durable replica-operation intent under the canonical operation-owner lifecycle; no coordinator-local waiter, TTL, secondary queue, or new metadata authority is allowed."},{"id":"dispatch-time-idle-proof","statement":"Physical self-move dispatch remains fail-closed until an authoritative incomplete-operation observation proves no other live conflict; unreadable or deferred visibility keeps the PENDING intent parked on canonical retry."},{"id":"no-interlock-weakening","statement":"Keep run-20 exclusive physical serialization, later-dependent deferral, run-22 quorum-spread ordering, and the emergency ADD exemption unchanged."},{"id":"lifecycle-owned-abandonment","statement":"Cancellation, transfer, retry, timeout, and cleanup reuse canonical operation-owner lease and reaper transitions; no raw age check deletes or bypasses a waiter."},{"id":"fairness-model","statement":"The fixed TLA+ contract must distinguish the durable waiting-writer turn from the admission-only starvation mutant, and npm run model:contracts must pass."},{"id":"behavioral-red-on-revert","statement":"On base bytes the focused test must explicitly observe legacy writer refusal, successfully admit later newcomers while no waiter is registered, and fail the named no-overtake assertion; fixed bytes must reject the same newcomers and retain incumbent, unreadable-visibility, and idle-release checks."},{"id":"no-live-workaround","statement":"Do not alter formation timeouts, polling or retry cadence, numeric budgets, workload, cluster size, activation predicates, remove safety, topology fences, or GCP ordering."},{"id":"ordered-live-gate","statement":"After deterministic proof, exact source verification, and checkpoint, run the unchanged dedicated five-node GCP formation/profile gate once and stop on its first red boundary."}],"verificationTemplates":[],"frontierIds":["operation-ledger-self-move-waiter-fairness-v3-main"]}}
